"First, we solve the equation $x(x-3)=1$. This can be rewritten as $x^2 - 3x - 1 = 0$.\n\nNext, we use the quadratic formula $x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}$, where $a = 1$, $b = -3$, and $c = -1$.\n\nPlugging in the values, we get:\n$$x = \\frac{-(-3) \\pm \\sqrt{(-3)^2 - 4(1)(-1)}}{2(1)} = \\frac{3 \\pm \\sqrt{9 + 4}}{2} = \\frac{3 \\pm \\sqrt{13}}{2}.$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $\\frac{3 + \\sqrt{13}}{2}$ and $\\frac{3 - \\sqrt{13}}{2}$.\n\nThe form $\\frac{a+\\sqrt{b}}{c}$ has $a = 3$, $b = 13$, and $c = 2$.\n\nTherefore, $abc = 3 \\cdot 13 \\cdot 2 = \\boxed{78}$."
"To find the value of \\( y^2 - 3xy + 8 \\) when \\((x, y) = (3, 9)\\), we will substitute \\( x = 3 \\) and \\( y = 9 \\) into the expression and simplify step by step.\n\n1. Substitute \\( x = 3 \\) and \\( y = 9 \\) into the expression:\n   \\[\n   y^2 - 3xy + 8 = 9^2 - 3(3)(9) + 8\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate \\( 9^2 \\):\n   \\[\n   9^2 = 81\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate \\( 3(3)(9) \\):\n   \\[\n   3(3)(9) = 81\n   \\]\n\n4. Substitute these values back into the expression:\n   \\[\n   81 - 81 + 8\n   \\]\n\n5. Perform the arithmetic:\n   \\[\n   81 - 81 + 8 = 8\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the answer is \\(\\boxed{8}\\)."
