"We can use the Shoelace Theorem to find the area of the quadrilateral. The Shoelace Theorem states that for a polygon with vertices $(x_1, y_1)$, $(x_2, y_2)$, ..., $(x_n, y_n)$, the area is given by:\n\n$$\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| \\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} (x_i y_{i+1} - y_ix_{i+1}) + (x_n y_1 - y_n x_1) \\right|$$\n\nApplying this formula to our vertices, we get:\n\n$$\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| (-1)(1) + (0)(0) + (2)(-3) + (0)(0) - (0)(0) - (1)(2) - (0)(-3) - (0)(-1) \\right| = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| -1 - 2 - 3 \\right| = \\boxed{4}$$\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $4$. I hope hope it is correct."
